PART 3 — ODD TANGENT FIELD x -> Sx
  odd n: rank(S) = n-1 always; ker S = span(w), adj(S) = w w^T (Pfaffian vector).
  full sphere S^4 is EVEN-dim: hairy ball forces a zero; zeros are exactly ±w/|w|.
  sum-zero sphere S^3 is ODD-dim: field x->Sx NONVANISHING there because
  sum(w) = sqrt(det(I+2A)) is ODD (never 0) => w not in 1^perp. Verify below.
  all w_i odd (never zero): True  [w_i = ±Pf(S minus i), Pf odd]
  sum(w) values (odd, = sqrt(det(I+2A))): [1, 3, 5, 7, 9]
  gcd(w) distribution: {1: 12}
  SIGN-SCORE LAW  sign(w_i)·(-1)^(s_i) constant per class: {'constant': 4, 'mixed': 8}
  MOD-4 LAW  w_i ≡ ±(-1)^(s_i) (mod 4) with one global sign: {'w_i ≡ ±(-1)^s_i mod 4 (global sign)': 12}
  Pearson corr(|w_i|, s_i): +0.0000
  Pearson corr(|w_i|, (s_i-mean)^2): +0.2384
  flow balance (S w = 0): for every vertex i, sum of w over out-neighbors
    equals sum of w over in-neighbors — w is the unique 'parity-balanced' weighting.
